      "problem": "Solve $-x^3-4x^2+5x+20=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we multiply the equation by $-1$ to make the coefficient of the cubic term positive. This gives\n\n$$\nx^3+4x^2-5x-20=0.\n$$\n\nWe then proceed to factor the left-hand side by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x-20 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}(x+4)-5(x+4) & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-5)(x+4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve $(x^2-5)(x+4)=0$ by setting each factor equal to $0.$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x^2-5)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =5 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Setting the factor $(x+4)$ equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions are $x=-4, \\pm \\sqrt 5.$",
